;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 (written by Claude, from design section 16 and
;; the guest runs; for the user's review). Why this is right:
;; - As expected-vax-rangechecks-1.err, but the traceback names the
;;   program section, POC_CODE, not RANGECHECKS_INIT: under -OC with
;;   -range-checks the fault is past about a kilobyte into the
;;   initializer, and VMS's traceback names a routine only that far (a
;;   guest test, 2026-10-10: a fault 907 bytes into a MACRO-32 routine
;;   is named by the routine, one 1107 bytes in by its section).
%SYSTEM-F-FLTOVF_F, arithmetic fault, floating overflow at PC=xxxxxxxx, PSL=xxxxxxxx
%TRACE-F-TRACEBACK, symbolic stack dump follows
module name     routine name                     line       rel PC    abs PC

RANGECHECKS     POC_CODE                                   xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
RANGECHECKS     RANGECHECKS_MAIN                           xxxxxxxx  xxxxxxxx
